  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="204f7fe2-38ef-5833-9cfa-a388e06ded2b" activityNameId="849225ba-b49e-5968-8b1c-d9f8fc7bd4fb" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Small hydropower plant, in waterworks infrastructure</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Small hydropower plant, in waterworks infrastructure
Average of three small hydropower plants. As parts of the infrastructure are already existing, the model is limited to the integration of material and energy. It basically consists of the integration of the turbine and generator into the existing constructions. The lifetime is assumed to be around 80 years. The data set describes a mix and is therefore not representative for individual plants. Sources: Baumgartner &amp; Doka (1998), Konersmann &amp; Jean-Baptiste (2000).;
UUID: 1c720264-c12f-3cb7-a7b2-b0b24acad63e
The dataset describes the construction of an average small hydropower plant integrated in an already existing waterworks infrastructure such as e.g. drinking water supply or irrigation system. It includes the materials used, the electricity and diesel consumed as well as the transports needed.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Average small hydropower plant integrated in existing infrastructure (e.g. drinking water supply, irrigation system). Capacity of 0.19MW
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_1c720264-c12f-3cb7-a7b2-b0b24acad63e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
